{title: Thine Be the Glory}
{artist: Edmond Budry; tr. R. B. Hoyle}
{genre: Easter}
{style: Hymn}
{flow: Closing}
{key: G}
{tempo: 96}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Thine be the glory, [D]risen, con[G]quering Son
[G]Endless is the vic[D]tory Thou o'er [G]death hast won
[G]Angels in bright [C]raiment rolled the [G]stone away
[Em]Kept the folded [D]graveclothes where Thy [G]body lay
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Thine be the glory, [D]risen, con[G]quering Son
[G]Endless is the vic[D]tory Thou o'er [G]death hast won
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Lo, Jesus meets us, [D]risen from the [G]tomb
[G]Lovingly He greets us, [D]scatters fear and [G]gloom
[G]Let the church with [C]gladness hymns of [G]triumph sing
[Em]For her Lord now [D]liveth, death hath lost its [G]sting
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]No more we doubt Thee, [D]glorious Prince of [G]life
[G]Life is nought with[D]out Thee, aid us in our [G]strife
[G]Make us more than [C]conquerors, through Thy deathless [G]love
[Em]Bring us safe through [D]Jordan to Thy home a[G]bove
{end_of_verse}
